# Applied by Workers Static Assets to every console response, the
# single-page fallback included. The console is never legitimately framed, and
# a page reached by client-side navigation — the OAuth consent page or the
# one-time reveal of a key, after signing in — never loads a document of its
# own whose headers a narrower rule could match. So one rule covers every path,
# and no path-specific frame rule may narrow it; console/src/headers.test.ts
# holds that.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
